<title>POLAND: Celuloza, Gorazdze to join WIG 20 index.</title>
<headline>Celuloza, Gorazdze to join WIG 20 index.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish paper firm Celuloza and cement maker Gorazdze will join the Warsaw bourse's large-cap WIG 20 index on July 16, replacing Animex and Exbud, the bourse's president said.</p>
<p>Wieslaw Rozlucki told a news conference that the next WIG 20 change in September could see the addition of Bank Handlowy and copper giant KGHM Polska Miedz, which starts bourse trade on July 10.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
